ts\\/2563\\/revisions\\/2769\"}],\"wp:attachment\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/media?parent=2563\"}],\"wp:term\":[{\"taxonomy\":\"category\",\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/categories?post=2563\"},{\"taxonomy\":\"post_tag\",\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/tags?post=2563\"}],\"curies\":[{\"name\":\"wp\",\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/api.w.org\\/{rel}\",\"templated\":true}]}}', '{\"source_id\":\"2563\",\"source_url\":\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/october-social-promoter-of-the-month-amy-grover\\/\",\"dest_id\":1058,\"dest_url\":\"http:\\/\\/localhost:8888\\/rnd\\/2018\\/09\\/25\\/october-social-promoter-of-the-month-amy-grover\\/\",\"title\":\"Social Promoter of the Month: Amy Grover\",\"author\":\"admin\",\"featured\":\"\",\"inline_images\":5,\"failed_images\":0,\"reused_images\":0,\"comments\":0,\"terms\":5,\"builders\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"fidelity\":\"rendered\",\"failed_urls\":[]}', '2026-08-27 11:01:25');
INSERT INTO `wp_ucm_queue` (`id`, `run_id`, `item_type`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `title`, `priority`, `status`, `attempts`, `dest_id`, `message`, `payload`, `result`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(388, 3, 'post', '2577', 'https://summitsalonacademy.edu/summit-owners-michael-and-karen-shea-lead-with-the-heart/', 'Summit Owners Michael and Karen Shea Lead With the Heart', 50, 'done', 1, 1059, '', '{\"id\":2577,\"date\":\"2018-10-18T11:48:57\",\"date_gmt\":\"2018-10-18T18:48:57\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/?p=2577\"},\"modified\":\"2024-05-13T10:55:55\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2024-05-13T17:55:55\",\"slug\":\"summit-owners-michael-and-karen-shea-lead-with-the-heart\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/summit-owners-michael-and-karen-shea-lead-with-the-heart\\/\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"Summit Owners Michael and Karen Shea Lead With the Heart\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">The beauty industry is full of talented people who want to make art, create relationships, and give back to the communities around them. At Summit Salon Academy our owners, <\\/span><a href=\\\"\\/about-us\\/staff\\/\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Michael and Karen Shea<\\/span><\\/a><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">, are perfect examples of this. With backgrounds in business, beauty, and education, this unstoppable team has been the driving force behind the school since its opening in 2006. From their dedication to students and the local community to their love of creativity and passion for the beauty industry, Michael and Karen have made Summit the incredible place that it is today.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Michael\\u2019s Background<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Michael Shea got into beauty at age 20, when he attended barber school during a pivotal period of change and modernization for the beauty industry. Michael chose barber school because it was more modern and cutting-edge than traditional beauty school at the time. After finishing school, he worked in a variety of different salons, eventually opening and owning his own business, Shea\\u2019s on Snelling, for 13 years. After this, Michael switched up his career path and worked for a beauty distribution company. \\u201cBeauty is a dynamic industry,\\u201d Michael says. \\u201cIt [the beauty industry] gives you the ability to stay as young as you want for as long as you want. It\\u2019s a state of mind.\\u201d Michael then began to work with the Summit Salon Business Center (SSBC), which is the world\\u2019s largest salon seminar, training, and consulting company. His work with SSBC required him to travel constantly and he was always proud to tell the people he met that he worked in the beauty industry. Working with this group is what initiated his jump into the world of school ownership.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Karen\\u2019s Background<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Unlike Michael, Karen didn\\u2019t plan on a career in beauty from a young age. Her passion was always in fashion and style, so she studied fashion marketing during college. After graduation, she worked in fashion retail for a while, but eventually ended up working with a local Northwest beauty distributor, Salon Services. During her seven years with this company, she worked various jobs, including outside sales representative, cosmetics line supervisor, and sales manager. Through this job, Karen learned the ins and outs of beauty and fell in love with the industry as a whole. \\u201cThere\\u2019s always something going on [in the beauty industry],\\u201d Karen says. \\u201cIt keeps your mind engaged. It\\u2019s never going to be a dull profession.\\u201d Her next career shift took her to a local art school, where she worked for 12 years in the admissions department. Though she didn\\u2019t know it at the time, her combined background of beauty and education would give her the tools she needed to own a beauty school later on.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Becoming Beauty School Owners<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Between the years of 2004 and 2010, hundreds of new beauty schools entered the industry. Old-fashioned schools were closing and new schools were paving the way with cutting-edge techniques and ideas. Between Michael\\u2019s experience in the salon business, Karen\\u2019s experience in education, and their shared background in beauty, the couple started to consider beauty school ownership in 2005. After many thorough discussions and help from SSBC, Karen and Michael decided to take the plunge. Summit Salon Academy opened in September 2006. Both agree that it\\u2019s one of the best decisions they\\u2019ve ever made.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><i><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">\\u201cIt was a very logical progression, even though we didn\\u2019t think so at the time,\\u201d Michael says.<\\/span><\\/i><\\/p>\\n<p><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/summit-owners-michael-and-karen-shea-lead-with-the-heart\\/img_1811\\/\\\" rel=\\\"attachment wp-att-2598\\\"><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" class=\\\"aligncenter wp-image-2598\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2018\\/10\\/IMG_1811-e1541007238585.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"Karen and Michael Shea.\\\" width=\\\"527\\\" height=\\\"706\\\" data-wp-editing=\\\"1\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2018\\/10\\/IMG_1811-e1541007238585.jpg 1936w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2018\\/10\\/IMG_1811-e1541007238585-224x300.jpg 224w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2018\\/10\\/IMG_1811-e1541007238585-768x1028.jpg 768w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2018\\/10\\/IMG_1811-e1541007238585-765x1024.jpg 765w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2018\\/10\\/IMG_1811-e1541007238585-299x400.jpg 299w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2018\\/10\\/IMG_1811-e1541007238585-448x600.jpg 448w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2018\\/10\\/IMG_1811-e1541007238585-550x736.jpg 550w\\\" sizes=\\\"auto, (max-width: 527px) 100vw, 527px\\\" \\/><\\/a><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Why Summit is Different<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Michael and Karen Shea have poured their heart and soul into Summit Salon Academy. This deep love and devotion is something that can be felt by students and staff members alike. \\u201cOur students\\u2019 lives are really big,\\u201d says Karen. \\u201cThey are all dealing with things. Sometimes we are the only soft place to land.\\u201d On the surface, students and staff members at Summit deal with the same challenges of any beauty school. However, when stressors, daily tasks, and common struggles are stripped away, there is an intentional purpose and passion for connection behind the school. \\u201d[Summit is] staff and students who are rallying together when bad things happen,\\u201d says Michael. \\u201cIt\\u2019s cool to watch students look out for each other and protect each other.\\u201d Behind the hair, makeup, and glamour, beauty is a giving industry with an enormous heart. At Summit, the Sheas work hard to set a good example for their students to not only help each other, but to give back to the community around them.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><i><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">\\u201dConnection and relationships are at the heart of why hairdressers choose this industry,\\u201d Michael and Karen say.<\\/span><\\/i><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">The Summit Family<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">At Summit, we believe in the idea of the &#8216;Summit Family,&#8217; where everyone feels like they belong. Here, students and staff become close friends, supporting each other through their journeys. This feeling of togetherness brings a lot of energy to our workplace and helps us work well together.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">The Summit Family isn&#8217;t just a concept; it&#8217;s a real thing that shows our shared values. When people feel connected and respected, they bring their best ideas and efforts to the table. This special atmosphere makes Summit Salon Academy Tacoma stand out, giving every member the chance to be their best selves.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<blockquote class=\\\"instagram-media\\\" style=\\\"background: #FFF; border: 0; border-radius: 3px; box-shadow: 0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width: 540px; min-width: 326px; padding: 0; width: calc(100% - 2px);\\\" data-instgrm-captioned=\\\"\\\" data-instgrm-permalink=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.instagram.com\\/p\\/C2I5keiv3Fn\\/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\\\" data-instgrm-version=\\\"14\\\">\\n<div style=\\\"padding: 16px;\\\">\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n<div style=\\\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center;\\\">\\n<div style=\\\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 40px; margin-right: 14px; width: 40px;\\\"><\\/div>\\n<div style=\\\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex-grow: 1; justify-content: center;\\\">\\n<div style=\\\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; margin-bottom: 6px; width: 100px;\\\"><\\/div>\\n<div style=\\\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; width: 60px;\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div style=\\\"padding: 19% 0;\\\"><\\/div>\\n<div style=\\\"display: block; height: 50px; margin: 0 auto 12px; width: 50px;\\\"><\\/div>\\n<div style=\\\"padding-top: 8px;\\\">\\n<div style=\\\"color: #3897f0; font-family: Arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 550; line-height: 18px;\\\">View this post on Instagram<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div style=\\\"padding: 12.5% 0;\\\"><\\/div>\\n<div style=\\\"disp