(432, 3, 'post', '4432', 'https://summitsalonacademy.edu/breast-cancer-awareness/', 'Breast Cancer Awareness', 50, 'done', 1, 1103, '', '{\"id\":4432,\"date\":\"2022-10-17T11:53:26\",\"date_gmt\":\"2022-10-17T18:53:26\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/?p=4432\"},\"modified\":\"2022-10-21T10:53:29\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2022-10-21T17:53:29\",\"slug\":\"breast-cancer-awareness\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/breast-cancer-awareness\\/\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"Breast Cancer Awareness\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">As part of our focus on Breast Cancer Awareness, we at Summit Salon Academy want to share inspiring stories from three amazing women: Sydney Berry, Talisa Boad, and Dannielle Varley. Each woman is an inspiration, showing such strength, courage and resilience.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Sydney Berry<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" class=\\\"aligncenter wp-image-4436\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/IMG_5917-300x300.png\\\" alt=\\\"sydney berry\\\" width=\\\"400\\\" height=\\\"400\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/IMG_5917-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/IMG_5917-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/IMG_5917-400x400.png 400w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/IMG_5917.png 408w\\\" sizes=\\\"auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Sydney has been in the beauty industry for over 50 years. During that time, she has held numerous positions including salon owner, salon consultant and owner of a multi-state distributorship \\u2013 Salon Services. She is currently the chair of PBA (Professional Beauty Association). Sydney is a recognized leader and mentor in the beauty industry. She has accomplished all this while tackling breast cancer. Sydney has battled multiple diagnosis of breast cancer over the past 32 years leading to 3 mastectomies and numerous treatments. She is currently living with Metastatic Breast Cancer with bone for seven years and to put it bluntly\\u2026she is a force of nature! Sydney\\u2019s positive mindset and resilience has shaped her journey living with Cancer.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Sydney has been a mentor to many who are going through the same experience. She believes in positivity, patience, and resilience as keys to overcoming this trial. She also knows that it\\u2019s\\u00a0<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">important to have a belief in your body\\u2019s ability to heal. Sydney\\u2019s advice is to \\u201csee your future. Recognize that you will have tough moments of challenge. [Listen to} how your body feels and\\u2026 seek out your community of support.\\u201d<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<h3><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">A \\u201cThriver\\u201d Mentality<\\/span><\\/h3>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Sydney doesn\\u2019t call herself a survivor; she is a THRIVER. Here\\u2019s what she has to say on the topic:<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">\\u201cA survivor mindset is one of negativity, struggle, darkness, defeat or win with a battlefield of setbacks. A [thriver\\u2019s] mentality is one of options\\u2026You are [prepared] to expect that downturns [can] lead to new options. It is a grace of lightness of being. [You are] the ONE in control of your reality. [It is] a choice\\u2013 Living in an actionable state of belief and response versus one of marching to your pre-determined destiny.\\u201d<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" class=\\\"aligncenter wp-image-4445 size-medium\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/image001-2-300x300.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"300\\\" height=\\\"300\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/image001-2-300x300.jpg 300w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/image001-2-150x150.jpg 150w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/image001-2-768x768.jpg 768w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/image001-2-400x400.jpg 400w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/image001-2-600x600.jpg 600w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/image001-2-550x550.jpg 550w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/image001-2.jpg 1024w\\\" sizes=\\\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n<h3><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">The Power of the Beauty Industry<\\/span><\\/h3>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Sydney knows the vital role the beauty industry plays for cancer patients as they make their own choice about how to deal with the impact of treatment on their body, especially the impact on a person\\u2019s hair. Sydney has been instrumental in raising funds for <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/hairtostay.org\\/\\\">HairToStay,<\\/a> a non-profit organization dedicated to helping cancer patients access innovative scalp cooling treatments with the aim to prevent hair loss due to chemotherapy. Sydney says, \\u201cWhen an oncologist delivers the news of chemotherapy as a treatment to cancer, you know you will lose your hair, and [you go] to the salon for a chemo cut.\\u201d\\u00a0 Because of her fundraising efforts for HairToStay, Sydney is being honored this month with the Cooler Heads Prevail Award at a gala fundraiser in San Francisco on October 9th.\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">To help put an end to \\u201cchemo cuts,\\u201d Summit Salon Academy is fundraising this month in Sydney\\u2019s honor. All proceeds will go towards the The Sydney Berry Fund within HairToStay. Sydney\\u2019s fund will be used to subsidize younger women (40 and under) who would otherwise be unable to afford scalp cooling. It will also support individuals employed directly or as independent contractors in the haircare and beauty industries.\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Talisa Boad<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" class=\\\"aligncenter wp-image-4434\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-169x300.jpeg\\\" alt=\\\"talisa and her client\\\" width=\\\"400\\\" height=\\\"711\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-169x300.jpeg 169w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-576x1024.jpeg 576w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-768x1365.jpeg 768w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-864x1536.jpeg 864w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-1152x2048.jpeg 1152w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-225x400.jpeg 225w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-338x600.jpeg 338w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8-550x978.jpeg 550w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/0B6A27AD-3459-411B-9A7E-299B017B20C8.jpeg 1242w\\\" sizes=\\\"auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Talisa Boad is a student at Summit Salon Academy who made the courageous decision to continue in school while fighting her recent diagnosis of Ovarian Cancer. During her treatment she found out that she is positive for the BRCA1 mutation gene \\u2013 a genetic marker for breast cancer. Due to the highly aggressive nature of the cancer she is currently fighting, Talisa will also undergo a mastectomy after the completion of her chemotherapy treatments<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Talisa has been brave and transparent in sharing her experience with cancer. \\u201cI am doing hair without hair. It\\u2019s a mixed bag of emotions.\\u00a0 I long for my blonde hair back. I long for curls as many clients do. I can empathize with clients who sit in my chair and have told me about their experience with their own cancer.\\u201d<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Talisa believes that, \\u201cwe can\\u2019t be afraid to talk about cancer and the effects it has on human lives because we can create better connections through open communication.\\u201d\\u00a0 \\u201cAfter I would finish a client&#8217;s service,\\u201d Talisa says, \\u201dI would often sit outside in exhaustion crying and feeling so weak. Many students came to talk with me. [They] hugged me and I thanked them for that support and thanked them for hugging me as I don\\u2019t often get hugs.\\u201d Through her experience, Talisa has created special bonds with her clients and fellow students.\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">As a single mother, being resilient is important in her life. She\\u2019s had to address issues and overcome them for years. Talisa says she has struggled on days during treatment \\u201cExcept when I was physically doing hair.\\u00a0 It made me feel so alive again. I Didn\\u2019t have any pains and I felt calm and a happiness inside me.\\u201d<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" class=\\\"aligncenter wp-image-4440 size-full\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/shutterstock_2035039004-1.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"400\\\" height=\\\"220\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/shutterstock_2035039004-1.jpg 400w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/shutterstock_2035039004-1-300x165.jpg 300w\\\" sizes=\\\"auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Talisa says \\u201call of my hard work I have done has been in honor of my children, classmates and my clients and for myself\\u2026.I finally did it, through all the experience, learning and knowledge, tears and fears, I truly am doing what I love the most.\\u00a0 This has been quite a long goal, that I never gave up on, regardless how hard life is\\/was. I will soon become a cancer survivor.\\u201d\\u00a0\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">We think you\\u2019re incredible, Talisa! \\u2013 and as of this blog post we are even more pleased to congratulate Talisa on her recent graduation from the Cosmetology course! We have no doubt Talisa is going to make an impact on so many lives as she works in the beauty industry.\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Dannielle Varley\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Dannielle started at Summit Salon Academy in July 2021. In Fall of 2021 she was diagnosed with stage 1B grade 3 triple negative breast cancer. She withdrew shortly after to pursue treatment which involved extensive chemotherapy and radiation prior to undergoing a double mastectomy and reconstructive surgery. Through it all Dannielle has stayed connected to her classmates and Summit Salon Academy and demonstrated such an amazing positive attitude.\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Cancer is \\u201cone thing I never thought I\\u2019d have or ever want anyone to ever go through,\\u201d Dannielle says, \\u201c[but I] have to try to keep a positive mindset. It\\u2019s not always easy but it is your best bet.\\u201d\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Dannielle says that her family is her biggest support system and helps her overcome her battles. Through her experience, she says \\u201cI stayed positive and always did my best to be me. Cancer wasn\\u2019t going to beat me.\\u201d\\u00a0 Since being diagnosed, Dannielle has discovered that there are so many ways to be beautiful. The beauty industry has shown her that services as simple as a manicure can help people feel good about themselves.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" class=\\\"aligncenter wp-image-4442 size-full\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/shutterstock_1697510932-1.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"breast cancer awareness bow\\\" width=\\\"602\\\" height=\\\"401\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/shutterstock_1697510932-1.jpg 602w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/shutterstock_1697510932-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/shutterstock_1697510932-1-600x400.jpg 600w, https:\\/\\/summitsalonacademy.edu\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2022\\/10\\/shutterstock_1697510932-1-550x366.jpg 550w\\\" sizes=\\\"auto, (max-width: 602px) 100vw, 602px\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Danielle shared \\u201cI miss my hair and I can\\u2019t wait till it is back, but this has been a learning experience. I\\u2019ve never been one to judge anyone and this just shows anything can happen to anyone. It is best to always get checked. I just turned 40 this year and I\\u2019m going to go back and finish school for hair because I love doing hair. I was so happy to be in school learning everything there is about hair.\\u201d<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">We are thrilled to report that Dannielle is now cancer-free and we are so looking forward to welcoming her back to Summit Salon Academy to complete her Cosmetology program! We are beyond proud of you, Dannielle!<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<h2><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Be A Part of the Solution<\\/span><\\/h2>\\n<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Help our students fundraise this month. During the month of October, when you visit <a href=\\\"\\/\\\">Summit Salon Academy<\\/a> for <a href=\\\"\\/guest-services\\/\\\">services<\\/a>, we will be donating part of the proceeds to HairToStay and the Sydney Berry Fund! <\\/span><\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>Breast Cancer Awareness Month is here, and we want to honor three incredible women. Sydney, Talisa, and Dannielle have all shown strength and resilience during their experiences with breast cancer. Learn more about them on our blog.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":4491,\"featured_media\":4433,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[187],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-4432\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"has-post-thumbnail\",\"hentry\",\"category-breast-cancer-awareness-month\"],\"acf\":[],\"aioseo_notices\":[],\"aioseo_head\":\"\\n\\t\\t<!-- All in One SEO 5.0.0.1 - aioseo.com -->\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"October is Breast Cancer Awareness Month, and we want to share the stories of three amazing women in the beauty industry. Read on to learn more about Sydney, Talisa, and Dannielle\\u2019s journeys.\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"max-snippet:-1, max-imag