(3693, 6, 'post', '673', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/press-releases/caller-in-crisis-survey', 'One of 911’s Toughest Challenges: Helping Callers in Crisis', 50, 'done', 1, 1178, '', '{\"id\":673,\"date\":\"2026-09-04T18:31:25\",\"date_gmt\":\"2026-09-04T18:31:25\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T06:06:29\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T06:06:29\",\"slug\":\"caller-in-crisis-survey\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"One of 911\\u2019s Toughest Challenges: Helping Callers in Crisis\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\\n<h3 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">As Americans increasingly expect 911 to provide help during mental health emergencies, especially suicide calls, a new IAED protocol is available to give Emergency Dispatchers the structure and tools for responding to callers in crisis\\u00a0<\\/h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><strong>September 4, 2026 (Salt Lake City, UT) <\\/strong>\\u2014 A new national survey conducted by the International Academies of Emergency Dispatch (IAED) reveals that Americans place significant trust in 911 Emergency Dispatchers during suicide-related and mental health emergencies and overwhelmingly expect them to have specialized training to handle these life-and-death calls.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">According to the survey of more than 1,500 Americans, 89% trust 911 Emergency Dispatchers to provide guidance during a suicide-related emergency, while 73% believe dispatchers actually receive specialized training to manage suicide risk calls. At the same time, 87% support providing Emergency Dispatchers with specialized training for suicide and mental health crisis situations.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The findings highlight a troubling disconnect between public expectations and reality.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Recognizing the urgent need for a consistent, evidence-based approach for handling these types of emergency calls, the IAED developed Protocol 41: Caller in Crisis (1st Party). Protocol 41 brings a new level of preparedness to emergency communications centers by providing IAED-certified Emergency Dispatchers with a structured calltaking protocol specifically for callers in crisis. With instructions for separating a caller from the means to do self-harm, and the Emotional Control Tool\\u2014a first-of-its-kind Pre-Arrival Instruction that gives Emergency Dispatchers mental state-specific techniques to deescalate situations where callers who are in personal crisis are overwhelmed by emotional or psychological distress\\u2014Protocol 41 enables dispatchers to offer immediate support, guide callers toward safety, and remain a calming presence during moments of personal crisis.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">&#8220;As this survey demonstrates, Americans clearly view 911 Emergency Dispatchers as a trusted source of guidance during some of life&#8217;s most critical moments,&#8221; said Jerry Overton, IAED President. \\u201cThe public expects dispatchers to be prepared for mental health emergencies, and Protocol 41 equips them with the right tools and training to meet those expectations.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Taking emergency calls from callers in crisis requires specialized skills and evidence-based procedures that many emergency communication professionals have not historically received through standard training programs. To help close this gap, the IAED developed Protocol 41: Caller in Crisis (1st Party Only), a specialized emergency communications protocol\\u2014the only one in the industry\\u2014designed to help Emergency Dispatchers effectively identify, support, and assist first party callers experiencing suicidal ideation, emotional distress, or other behavioral health crises.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Released in 2024 and now with almost 10,000 trained Emergency Dispatchers, Protocol 41 provides structured guidance that enables Emergency Dispatchers to help callers in crisis while at the same time supporting dispatcher wellness and resilience. By providing a clear, evidence-based framework for managing these complex and emotionally challenging calls, the protocol reduces uncertainty, cognitive burden, and the risk of second-guessing difficult decisions after the call has ended.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u201cBy having this Protocol, you have given your Emergency Dispatchers a tool to alleviate somebody else\\u2019s trauma, to alleviate somebody else\\u2019s PTSD, to immediately intervene, and when they\\u2019re in their darkest place to literally give them hope, give them a way forward,\\u201d said Jonathan Flynn, the Training and Compliance Specialist for Allina Health Emergency Medical Services in St. Paul, Minnesota. \\u201cSince we implemented Protocol 41, I have yet to have a staff member come to me saying, like, hey, I had a really bad first-party mental health call, and I don&#8217;t know how to deal with it.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">As awareness of mental health challenges continues to grow nationwide, the survey findings underscore the need for consistent, specialized crisis intervention training for those who often serve as the first point of contact during an emergency. Truly a \\u201czero-response time\\u201d solution is now available.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/s\\/c8vbjm8g8c\\/national-suicide-month-survey-results-downloadable\\\">Click here<\\/a> to download the complete survey results.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Learn more about Protocol 41: Caller in Crisis <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/get.prioritydispatch.net\\/protocol-41\\/\\\">here<\\/a>.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h4 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">About the IAED:&nbsp;<\\/h4>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch is the standard-setting organization for medical, fire, police, and nurse triage emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and is the leading body of emergency services dispatch experts. emergencydispatch.org<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h4 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">About Priority Dispatch:\\u00a0<\\/h4>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Priority Dispatch\\u2122 is the world leader in providing research-based protocol solutions to emergency call centers in medical, fire, police, and nurse triage disciplines for over 45 years. Get to know us at prioritydispatch.net.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>A new national survey conducted by the International Academies of Emergency Dispatch (IAED) reveals that Americans place significant trust in 911 Emergency Dispatchers during suicide-related and mental health emergencies and overwhelmingly expect them to have specialized training to handle these life-and-death calls.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[22],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-673\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-press-releases\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>One of 911\\u2019s Toughest Challenges: Helping Callers in Crisis | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"One of 911\\u2019s Toughest Challenges: Helping Callers in Crisis | Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"A new national survey conducted by the International Academies of Emergency Dispatch (IAED) reveals that Americans place significant trust in 911 Emergency Dispatchers during suicide-related and mental health emergencies and overwhelmingly expect them to have specialized training to handle these life-and-death calls.\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:site_name\\\" content=\\\"Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:published_time\\\" content=\\\"2026-09-04T18:31:25+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:modified_time\\\" content=\\\"2026-10-19T06:06:29+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"author\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:card\\\" content=\\\"summary_large_image\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:label1\\\" content=\\\"Written by\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data1\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:label2\\\" content=\\\"Est. reading time\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data2\\\" content=\\\"4 minutes\\\" \\/>\\n<script type=\\\"application\\/ld+json\\\" class=\\\"yoast-schema-graph\\\">{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\\",\\\"@graph\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Article\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-releases\\\\\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\\\\\\/#article\\\",\\\"isPartOf\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-releases\\\\\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\\\\\\/\\\"},\\\"author\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/#\\\\\\/schema\\\\\\/person\\\\\\/338f35ee363eca7c9019764391474b5a\\\"},\\\"headline\\\":\\\"One of 911\\u2019s Toughest Challenges: Helping Callers in Crisis\\\",\\\"datePublished\\\":\\\"2026-09-04T18:31:25+00:00\\\",\\\"dateModified\\\":\\\"2026-10-19T06:06:29+00:00\\\",\\\"mainEntityOfPage\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-releases\\\\\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\\\\\\/\\\"},\\\"wordCount\\\":695,\\\"commentCount\\\":0,\\\"articleSection\\\":[\\\"Press Releases\\\"],\\\"inLanguage\\\":\\\"en-US\\\",\\\"potentialAction\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"CommentAction\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Comment\\\",\\\"target\\\":[\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-releases\\\\\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\\\\\\/#respond\\\"]}]},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"WebPage\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-releases\\\\\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\\\\\\/\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-releases\\\\\\/caller-in-crisis-survey\\\\\\/\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"One of 911\\u2019s Toughest Challenges: Helping Callers in Crisis | Emergency Dispatch\\\",\\\"isPartOf\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/#website\\\"},\\\"datePublished\\\":\\\"2026-09-04T18:31:25+00:00\\\",\\\"dateModified\\\":\\\"2026-10-19T06:06:29+00:00\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/#\\\\\\/schema\\\\\\/person\\\\\\/338f35ee363eca7c901