(3694, 6, 'post', '674', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/press-releases/E5554F73-6C34-4884-AFCF-7E03D9E9D497', 'IAED, Priority Solutions Inc., and the Welsh Ambulance Service Agree to Commercialise the Call Prioritisation Streaming System (CPSS)', 50, 'done', 1, 1179, '', '{\"id\":674,\"date\":\"2026-08-24T18:13:05\",\"date_gmt\":\"2026-08-24T18:13:05\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/cpss\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T06:07:54\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T06:07:54\",\"slug\":\"e5554f73-6c34-4884-afcf-7e03d9e9d497\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/E5554F73-6C34-4884-AFCF-7E03D9E9D497\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"IAED, Priority Solutions Inc., and the Welsh Ambulance Service Agree to Commercialise the Call Prioritisation Streaming System (CPSS)\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"<h3>Proven Non-Emergency Clinical Triage Solution Will Improve Patient Access and Free Up Emergency Medical Response Resources<\\/h3>\\n<p><strong>Salt Lake City, Utah and Wales <\\/strong>\\u2014 August 24, 2026 \\u2014 The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch (IAED), Priority Solutions Inc. (PSI), and Welsh Ambulance Services University NHS Trust (WAST) announced today that they have signed an intellectual property agreement for the Call Prioritisation Streaming System (CPSS), paving the way for global commercialization of the clinically proven non-emergency telephone triage system.<\\/p>\\n<p>\\u201cModern ambulance services, internationally, respond to a broad spectrum of patient acuity, with a large percentage of 999 calls relating to conditions that are not immediately life-threatening and can be managed through alternative clinical pathways,\\u201d explains Dr. Conrad Fivaz, President, Priority Solutions Inc. \\u201cFor this reason, we\\u2019re excited to bring CPSS to healthcare organizations worldwide. This proven solution we\\u2019ve built together with WAST and the IAED is going to help improve patient access and care by optimizing resources, for callers with non-life-threatening and life-threatening symptoms alike.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>CPSS was developed within the 111 system and first deployed by <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/111.wales.nhs.uk\\/?locale=en&amp;term=A\\\">NHS 111 Wales<\\/a> on April 30, 2024. Priority Solutions Inc. helped transform CPSS into a scalable solution for health systems that take urgent but non-life-threatening calls or messages directly from the public.<\\/p>\\n<p>Designed for services such as 111, 1450, nurse advice lines, and integrated urgent care, CPSS enables trained non-clinical call takers to safely prioritise patients and direct them to the most appropriate care pathway. By accurately identifying callers with potential life-threatening symptoms, the system helps reduce demand on clinical resources that are often scarce, while still ensuring patients receive timely access to appropriate care.<\\/p>\\n<p>&#8220;CPSS is built on decades of frontline non-clinical telephone triage experience and continues to evolve through evidence, research, and user feedback,\\u201d stated Dr. Mike Brady, Assistant Clinical Director for Remote Clinical Care, Welsh Ambulance Services University NHS Trust. \\u201cHealth services everywhere are facing rising demand and limited clinical resources, and CPSS was designed to help meet that challenge by supporting safe, efficient non-clinical patient prioritization.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<p>The partnership combines WAST&#8217;s decades of operational experience in telephone triage, PSI&#8217;s LowCode technology platform and Emergency Communication Nurse System (ECNS), and IAED&#8217;s internationally recognized clinical governance framework. IAED will oversee ongoing protocol governance through its established Proposals for Change process and Council of Standards, ensuring CPSS continues to evolve through evidence-based medicine, operational experience, and user feedback.<\\/p>\\n<p>CPSS is a call-handler-led process that prioritises and streams patients following initial triage. While it has traditionally been used to care for suitable lower acuity patients for alternative management pathways, its application has broadened to support the prioritisation and streaming of a wider range of patients for further assessment and decision-making within the emergency care system.<\\/p>\\n<p>CPSS is ideally suited for healthcare organizations seeking to optimize clinician capacity, improve patient navigation, and safely manage growing demand for urgent care services. For agencies already using ProQA\\u00ae who are Accredited Centers of Excellence with the IAED, CPSS complements existing workflows such as PSI\\u2019s ECNS system. Organizations not using ProQA can implement CPSS with PSI\\u2019s Emergency Communication Nurse System (ECNS).<\\/p>\\n<p>###<\\/p>\\n<h4>SUPPORTING DATA:<\\/h4>\\n<p>Independently peer-reviewed research validating the system&#8217;s clinical performance includes a <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com\\/?url=https%3A%2F%2Finnovations.bmj.com%2Fcontent%2F11%2F2%2F89&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cwendy.whittaker%40prioritydispatch.net%7C80bdf5b78c434c81a73e08dee9e2c5a5%7C4aecbac934be4328a2ad28c8d2fc3127%7C0%7C0%7C639205357362391389%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=FAu%2BbozPFlpHhNU%2FBtYKlEm%2BbDTt4hpDNfcUWRjiiIw%3D&amp;reserved=0\\\">2025 publication in BMJ<\\/a> Innovations that documented the development of CPSS and reported that the platform had already managed more than 530,000 patient cases, demonstrating both its maturity and real-world operational capability. Since the 2024 go-live, CPSS has now managed over 1.6 million calls.<\\/p>\\n<p>A second <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com\\/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbmjopen.bmj.com%2Fcontent%2F15%2F7%2Fe097914&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cwendy.whittaker%40prioritydispatch.net%7C80bdf5b78c434c81a73e08dee9e2c5a5%7C4aecbac934be4328a2ad28c8d2fc3127%7C0%7C0%7C639205357362352221%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=1C8woOzS4OcystFc3geF%2F9Vgz5PZDk1rfF4fXjIgiKc%3D&amp;reserved=0\\\">2025 BMJ Open evaluation<\\/a> was performed where 83.4% of cases achieved expert clinical consensus on the appropriateness of CPSS outcomes, while clinicians agreed with those outcomes 90.5% of the time when consensus was reached. The study concluded that no significant clinical safety concerns were identified, providing confidence to patients, healthcare providers, and system stakeholders.<\\/p>\\n<h4>ABOUT PRIORITY SOLUTIONS, INC.:<\\/h4>\\n<p>Our LowCode software technology contains a base set of research-based and clinically proven protocols that have been used in more than 100,000,000 calls world-wide for over 26 years. LowCode supports ECNS and CPSS, solutions designed to provide better care to non-emergency callers while freeing up response resources and emergency lines for life-threatening calls that need the most attention. <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritysolutionsinc.com\\/\\\">prioritysolutionsinc.com<\\/a><\\/p>\\n<h4>ABOUT WAST:<\\/h4>\\n<p>Welsh Ambulance Services University NHS Trust provides emergency and urgent healthcare services for people across Wales, delivering high quality and patient-led clinical care, wherever and whenever needed. WAST services include call taking, remote clinical consultation, and conveyance to an appropriate hospital or alternative treatment facility, if needed. Non-Emergency Patient Transport Service (NEPTS) takes patients to and from hospital appointments and transfers them between hospitals and treatment facilities. NHS 111 Wales provides healthcare advice 24\\/7 for those feeling unwell who aren&#8217;t sure where to go for help. WAST also supports Community First Responders, Co-Responders and Uniformed Responders to provide additional resources for those most in need of help in our communities. <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/ambulance.nhs.wales\\/\\\">ambulance.nhs.wales<\\/a><\\/p>\\n<h4>ABOUT THE IAED:<\\/h4>\\n<p>The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch is the standard-setting organization for medical, fire, police, and nurse triage emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and is the leading body of emergency services dispatch experts. Our various Boards and Councils work on behalf of over 83,000 members in 60 countries\\u2014and in coordination with other influential public safety organizations\\u2014to ensure that the comprehensive system covering all aspects of emergency dispatching is safe, fast, effective, and cutting-edge. IAED protocols are used in more than 4,257 communication centers across the world in 31 languages and have been time-tested across hundreds of millions of calls for medical, fire, police, and nurse triage dispatching. <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/home\\\">emergencydispatch.org<\\/a><br \\/>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch (IAED), Priority Solutions Inc. (PSI), and Welsh Ambulance Services University NHS Trust (WAST) announced today that they have signed an intellectual property agreement for the Call Prioritisation Streaming System (CPSS), paving the way for global commercialization of the clinically proven non-emergency telephone triage system.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[22],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-674\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-press-releases\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>IAED, Priority Solutions Inc., and the Welsh Ambulance Service Agree to Commercialise the Call Prioritisation Streaming System (CPSS) | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"IAED, Priority Solutions Inc., and the Welsh Ambulance Service Agree to Commercialise the Call Prioritisation Streaming System (CPSS) | Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch (IAED), Priority Solutions Inc. (PSI), and Welsh Ambulance Services University NHS Trust (WAST) announced today that they have signed an intellectual property agreement for the Call Prioritisation Streaming System (CPSS), paving the way for global commercialization of the clinically proven non-emergency telephone triage system.\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/E5554F73-6C34-4884-AFCF-7E03D9E9D497\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:site_name\\\" content=\\\"Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:published_time\\\" content=\\\"2026-08-24T18:13:05+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:modified_time\\\" content=\\\"2026-10-19T06:07:54+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<