(3712, 6, 'post', '692', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/press-releases/D3271550-CFAD-4132-90BE-24116BD42964', 'IAED RELEASES LANDMARK EVOLUTION OF EMERGENCY FIRE PROTOCOLS WITH FPDS V8.0', 50, 'done', 1, 1197, '', '{\"id\":692,\"date\":\"2024-11-26T21:26:48\",\"date_gmt\":\"2024-11-26T21:26:48\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/D3271550-CFAD-4132-90BE-24116BD42964\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T07:45:31\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T07:45:31\",\"slug\":\"d3271550-cfad-4132-90be-24116bd42964\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/D3271550-CFAD-4132-90BE-24116BD42964\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"IAED RELEASES LANDMARK EVOLUTION OF EMERGENCY FIRE PROTOCOLS WITH FPDS V8.0\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\\n<p class=\\\"PageNumberFooter wp-block-paragraph\\\"><strong>FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE: NOVEMBER 26, 2024<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><strong>Contact for IAED<\\/strong><br>Pam Stewart, Senior Director of Operations<br>800.363.9127 ext. 131<br><a href=\\\"mailto:pam.stewart@emergencydispatch.org\\\">pam.stewart@emergencydispatch.org<\\/a><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><strong>Contact for Priority Dispatch<\\/strong><br>Brian Dale, President\\u00a0<br>385.236.4561<br><a href=\\\"mailto:brian.dale@prioritydispatch.net\\\">brian.dale@prioritydispatch.net<\\/a><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">SALT LAKE CITY, UT<i>&nbsp;<\\/i>\\u2013 Priority Dispatch\\u00ae and the International Academies of Emergency Dispatch are proud to announce the release of FPDS<code>\\u00ae<\\/code> v8.0, the landmark update of the Fire Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (FPDS\\u00ae) designed to bring critical enhancements to emergency fire dispatch. This significant evolution modernizes and expands the FPDS protocols, equipping Emergency Fire Dispatchers with powerful tools to meet the demands of today\\u2019s complex fire and rescue environments.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">With input from users around the world, FPDS v8.0 features updates to 32 of 34 protocols, including new instructions for managing emerging threats like electric vehicle fires and extreme weather incidents. Two new protocols\\u2014Protocol H, for on-scene medical assessment and treatment, and Protocol V, for assisting callers trapped in vehicles on fire\\u2014have been added to enhance civilian and responder safety during high-risk events.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">&#8220;We\\u2019re incredibly grateful to the agencies who submitted over 210 Proposals for Change based on their real-world experience with the FPDS,\\u201d said Mike Thompson, Chair of the IAED\\u2122 Curriculum Board and member of the Fire Standards Council. \\u201cOver 150 of their proposals were included, helping us refine the FPDS to address the growing complexities and dangers of fire\\/rescue incidents.<span>&nbsp; <\\/span>This update will enable dispatchers to develop more precise information and give expanded instructions to help keep their communities safe and ensure Fire Departments have the information they need to respond.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">This release also introduces a revised HAZMAT protocol, enabling dispatchers to provide civilian-directed decontamination guidance in specific situations and offers expanded options for callers in sinking vehicles. Protocol H, based on the standards from the Medical Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (MPDS\\u00ae), equips fire dispatchers with medical instructions for essential interventions, such as bleeding control and airway positioning, enhancing response during critical moments.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u201cFPDS v8.0 represents a new era in fire dispatch, building on the best ideas from both our dedicated users and our team of protocol experts,\\u201d said Brian Dale, Former Salt Lake City Fire Chief and President of Priority Dispatch. \\u201cWe\\u2019re thrilled to offer this update to our community of users across the world, empowering them to provide the best possible response to every call.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\\\">###<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;\\\"><strong>About<\\/strong><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12.0pt;letter-spacing:.5pt;line-height:115%;\\\"><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;\\\"><strong>the<\\/strong><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12.0pt;letter-spacing:.55pt;line-height:115%;\\\"><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12.0pt;letter-spacing:-.1pt;line-height:115%;\\\"><strong>IAED:<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch is the standard-setting organization for medical, fire, police, and nurse triage emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and is the leading body of emergency services dispatch experts. Our various Boards and Councils work on behalf of over 69,000 members in 59 countries\\u2014and in coordination with other influential public safety organizations\\u2014to ensure that the comprehensive system covering all aspects of emergency dispatching is safe, fast, effective, and cutting-edge. IAED protocols are used in more than 4,142 communication centers across the world and have been time-tested <span>across hundreds of millions of calls for medical, fire, police, and nurse triage dispatching. Learn more at&nbsp;<\\/span><a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/home\\\"><span>emergencydispatch.org<\\/span><\\/a><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span><strong>About<\\/strong><\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:.55pt;\\\"><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/span><span><strong>Priority<\\/strong><\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:.6pt;\\\"><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.1pt;\\\"><strong>Dispatch:<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span>Priority Dispatch<\\/span><span style=\\\"position:relative;top:-3.5pt;\\\">\\u2122<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:1.9pt;position:relative;top:-3.5pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>is the world leader in providing research-based protocol solutions to emergency call centers in medical, fire, police, and nurse triage disciplines. For over 44 years, EMS and 911 agencies have used the Medical Priority Dispatch System<\\/span><span style=\\\"position:relative;top:-3.5pt;\\\">\\u2122<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:1.9pt;position:relative;top:-3.5pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>(MPDS<\\/span><span style=\\\"position:relative;top:-3.5pt;\\\">\\u00ae<\\/span><span>), initially with cardsets and now only<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>fully<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>represented<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>in<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>ProQA<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>software.<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>Our<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>solutions<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>have<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>been<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>time-tested<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>in<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>30<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>languages<\\/span><span style=\\\"letter-spacing:-.3pt;\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><span>across hundreds of millions of calls and serve communities in thousands of agencies in 59 countries. Get to know us at&nbsp;<\\/span><a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.prioritydispatch.net\\/en\\\"><span>prioritydispatch.net<\\/span><\\/a><\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>FPDS V8.0 is designed to bring critical modern enhancements to emergency fire dispatch, equipping Emergency Fire Dispatchers with powerful tools to meet the demands of today\\u2019s complex fire and rescue environments.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[22],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-692\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-press-releases\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>IAED RELEASES LANDMARK EVOLUTION OF EMERGENCY FIRE PROTOCOLS WITH FPDS V8.0 | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"IAED RELEASES LANDMARK EVOLUTION OF EMERGENCY FIRE PROTOCOLS WITH FPDS V8.0 | Emergency Dispatch\\