(3722, 6, 'post', '702', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/press-releases/E2D70224-3AFD-4CB7-B3CA-481B5F0EFF2B', 'IAED Unveils Protocol 40 and Enhanced Protocols Across Police, Fire, and Medical Disciplines', 50, 'done', 1, 1207, '', '{\"id\":702,\"date\":\"2023-11-16T23:09:02\",\"date_gmt\":\"2023-11-16T23:09:02\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/E2D70224-3AFD-4CB7-B3CA-481B5F0EFF2B\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T08:10:44\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T08:10:44\",\"slug\":\"e2d70224-3afd-4cb7-b3ca-481b5f0eff2b\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/E2D70224-3AFD-4CB7-B3CA-481B5F0EFF2B\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"IAED Unveils Protocol 40 and Enhanced Protocols Across Police, Fire, and Medical Disciplines\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u2122 (IAED<strong><sup>\\u00ae<\\/sup><\\/strong>) is pleased to announce the groundbreaking Protocol 40: Incident Standby\\/Staging, along with comprehensive updates to the Police Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (PPDS<strong><sup>\\u00ae<\\/sup><\\/strong>), Fire Priority Dispatch System\\u2122<sup> <\\/sup>(FPDS<strong><sup>\\u00ae<\\/sup><\\/strong>), and Medical Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (MPDS<strong><sup>\\u00ae<\\/sup><\\/strong>) protocols.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\"><strong>Protocol 40: Incident Standby\\/Staging<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">Developed by the IAED, Protocol 40 addresses the diverse standby requests EMS agencies receive without reported patients at the scene. This protocol empowers agencies to efficiently process, assign, and document varied responses to each unique request for service. ProQA v5.1.1.48 includes a Special Procedures Briefing for Protocol 40. <\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\"><strong>MPDS v14.0.137<\\/strong><strong><span style=\\\"background-color:white\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">&nbsp;(10\\/18\\/2023)<\\/span><\\/span><\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">The Medical Priority Dispatch System sees significant updates in version 14.0.137. The clarifiers related to SERIOUS hemorrhage have been refined, and Protocol 23: Overdose\\/Poisoning now includes new answer choices and suffixes to distinguish between accidental and intentional substance intake.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\"><strong>FPDS v7.1.244 <\\/strong><strong><span style=\\\"background-color:white\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">(9\\/28\\/2023)<\\/span><\\/span><\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">The Fire Priority Dispatch System receives notable adjustments in version 7.1.244, enhancing Case Entry definitions, Chief Complaint Selection Rules, and refining wording for various Key Questions in Protocol 69: Structure Fire. These improvements contribute to clearer communication and more accurate responses in fire-related emergencies.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\"><strong>PPDS v7.0.348 <\\/strong><strong><span style=\\\"background-color:white\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">(10\\/27\\/2023)<\\/span><\\/span><\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">The Police Priority Dispatch System version 7.0.348 includes the addition of two agency-defined Critical EPD Information (CEIs) for every Chief Complaint. Protocol 106: Assault\\/Sexual Assault\\/Shooting\\/Stabbing now enables suffixes E and U for all STABBING codes, offering more detailed coding options.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">The IAED remains committed to supporting emergency dispatchers and responders as they serve their communities. These protocol updates reflect our dedication to continual evolution, ensuring the highest standard of care. The release includes training, certification, and ongoing education to empower Emergency Dispatchers, enhancing efficiency, safety, and community confidence.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u00a0<span style=\\\"color:black\\\">For the full email communication regarding these release details, click <span style=\\\"color:#00b0f0\\\">here<\\/span>.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\"><strong>About the IAED<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black\\\">The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch<sup>\\u00ae<\\/sup> (IAED\\u2122) is a nonprofit, standard-setting organization promoting safe and effective emergency dispatch services worldwide. The IAED has over 40 protocol-based research studies published in peer-reviewed journals and provides over 304,281 active medical, police, fire, and nurse dispatch certifications globally. The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch is the leading body of emergency services dispatch experts with various Boards and Councils that work on behalf of over 69,000 members in 59 countries\\u2014and in coordination with other influential public safety organizations\\u2014to ensure that the comprehensive system covering all aspects of emergency dispatching is safe, fast, effective, and cutting-edge. IAED protocols are used in more than 4,080 communication centers across the world and have been time-tested across hundreds of millions of calls for medical, fire, police, and nurse triage dispatching.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u2122 (IAED\\u00ae) is pleased to announce the groundbreaking Protocol 40: Incident Standby\\/Staging, along with comprehensive updates to the Police Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (PPDS\\u00ae), Fire Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (FPDS\\u00ae), and Medical Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (MPDS\\u00ae) protocols.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[22],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-702\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-press-releases\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>IAED Unveils Protocol 40 and Enhanced Protocols Across Police, Fire, and Medical Disciplines | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"IAED Unveils Protocol 40 and Enhanced Protocols Across Police, Fire, and Medical Disciplines | Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u2122 (IAED\\u00ae) is pleased to announce the groundbreaking Protocol 40: Incident Standby\\/Staging, along with comprehensive updates to the Police Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (PPDS\\u00ae), Fire Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (FPDS\\u00ae), and Medical Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (MPDS\\u00ae) protocols.\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/E2D70224-3AFD-4CB7-B3CA-481B5F0EFF2B\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:site_name\\\" content=\\\"Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:published_time\\\" content=\\\"2023-11-16T23:09:02+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:modified_time\\\" content=\\\"2026-10-19T08:10:44+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"author\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:card\\\" content=\\\"summary_large_image\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:label1\\\" content=\\\"Written by\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data1\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:label2\\\" content=\\\"Est. reading time\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data2\\\" content=\\\"2 minutes\\\" \\/>\\n<script type=\\\"application\\/ld+json\\\" class=\\\"yoast-schema-graph\\\">{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\\",\\\"@graph\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Article\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-releases\\\\\\/E2D70224-3AFD-4CB7-B3CA-481B5F0EFF2B\\\\\\/#article\\\",\\\"isPartOf\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-releases\\\\\\/E2D70224-3AFD-4CB7-B3CA-481B5F0EFF2B\\\\\\/\\\"},\\\"author\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/#\\\\\\/schema\\\\\\/person\\\\\\/338f35ee363eca7c9019764391474b5a\\\"},\\\"headline\\\":\\\"IAED Unveils Protocol 40 and Enhanced Protocols Across Police, Fire, and Medical Disciplines\\\",\\\"datePublished\\\":\\\"2023-11-16T23:09:02+00:00\\\",\\\"dateModified\\\":\\\"2026-10-19T08:10:44+00:00\\\",\\\"mainEntityOfPage\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/press-release