(3724, 6, 'post', '704', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/press-releases/963B3265-C780-447D-A040-053CD7C51958', 'The Hidden Emergency Crisis: 9-1-1 Staffing Is a Challenge in Many Communities', 50, 'done', 1, 1209, '', '{\"id\":704,\"date\":\"2023-06-21T00:09:57\",\"date_gmt\":\"2023-06-21T00:09:57\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/963B3265-C780-447D-A040-053CD7C51958\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T08:05:20\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T08:05:20\",\"slug\":\"963b3265-c780-447d-a040-053cd7c51958\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/963B3265-C780-447D-A040-053CD7C51958\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"The Hidden Emergency Crisis: 9-1-1 Staffing Is a Challenge in Many Communities\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><strong>Report finds more than one-third of nation\\u2019s call centers significantly understaffed with call demand surging<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">SALT LAKE CITY (June 12, 2023) \\u2013 The results from a recently released <a style=\\\"color:#0563c1;text-decoration:underline;\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/press-releases\\/d1ff0c4c-38ca-4e4f-8a96-cb6d9f2e5f63\\\">survey<\\/a> of the workforce staffing emergency call centers are sobering. Of 774 9-1-1 call centers around the United States, 36% reported vacancy rates that exceeded 30% of staffing levels, with 166 of those centers reporting rates above 40%.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The highest vacancy rate reported in 2022 actually reached 83%. The 25 centers reporting the greatest losses are located in all regions of the country, and the average vacancy rate \\u2013 25 percent \\u2013 is similar across all sizes of agencies.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The International Academies or Emergency Dispatch (IAED) and the National Association of State 9-1-1 Administrators (NASNA) released this week the updated report<i>, America\\u2019s 911 Workforce In Crisis<\\/i>. Survey responses reveal that 9-1-1 staffing shortages are affecting all parts of the country and all sizes of call centers.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u201cWhen there are more incoming demands on the 9-1-1 center than there are trained, qualified personnel to respond, public safety is put at risk,\\u201d said Ty Wooten, director of government affairs for the International Academies of Emergency Dispatch (IAED).<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">An accompanying analysis of news stories from around the country in the first half of 2023 found more than a dozen communities reeling from staffing vacancies from Maine to Hawaii, and more are being reported nearly every week.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The workforce crisis is occurring at a time when 9-1-1 telecommunicators are fielding more calls each year. Among the findings:<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\\"wp-block-list\\\">\\n<li>36% of call centers reported having fewer positions filled in 2022 than in 2019.<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Nearly one-third reported stunning vacancy rates in 2022: 13 reported that 70% or more of positions were unfilled; 92 reported a vacancy rate between 50-69%; and 166 reported rates of 30% to 49%.<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Nearly 4,000 staff departures were recorded in one year collectively among the centers. Departing staff with at least one year of experience cited pay, work hours, and stress as reasons for leaving.<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Only 27% of centers reported no change in actual staffing levels over the most recent 4-year period.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u201cAn alarming number of 911 centers are experiencing their own workforce emergencies,\\u201d said Harriet Rennie-Brown, executive director of NASNA. \\u201cWe need better workforce recruitment, retention, and support to ensure the quality of the 911 emergency services we all rely on.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Workforce challenges are expected to be a major topic of discussion at the upcoming annual conference for NENA \\u2013 The 9-1-1 Association in Grapevine, Texas, where Wooten will be speaking about the subject on June 19.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div>\\n<p><i><strong>America\\u2019s 911 Workforce In Crisis<\\/strong><\\/i><strong> report is available at <\\/strong><a style=\\\"color:#0563c1;text-decoration:underline;\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/press-releases\\/d1ff0c4c-38ca-4e4f-8a96-cb6d9f2e5f63\\\"><strong>www.EmergencyDispatch.org under News.<\\/strong><\\/a><strong> A graphic of the range of stunning vacancy rates is available.<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><i>IAED is the standard-setting organization for emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and is the leading body of emergency dispatch experts. Learn more at <\\/i><a style=\\\"color:#0563c1;text-decoration:underline;\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.EmergencyDispatch.org\\\"><i>www.EmergencyDispatch.org<\\/i><\\/a><i>.<\\/i><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><i>The National Association of State 911 Administrators (NASNA) is the voice of the states on public policy issues impacting 911. Learn more at <\\/i><a style=\\\"color:#0563c1;text-decoration:underline;\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nasna.org\\\"><i>nasna911.org<\\/i><\\/a><i>.<\\/i><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Review and download the&nbsp;<a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/s\\/kmwkvgqfdx\\/iaed_nasna_staffing-survey-report-2023\\\">full survey report<\\/a>&nbsp;for all of the details.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>The results from a recently released survey of the workforce staffing emergency call centers are sobering. Of 774 9-1-1 call centers around the United States, 36% reported vacancy rates that exceeded 30% of staffing levels, with 166 of those centers reporting rates above 40%.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[22],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-704\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-press-releases\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>The Hidden Emergency Crisis: 9-1-1 Staffing Is a Challenge in Many Communities | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"The Hidden Emergency Crisis: 9-1-1 Staffing Is a Challenge in Many Communities | Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"The results from a recently released survey of the workforce staffing emergency call centers are sobering. Of 774 9-1-1 call centers around the United States, 36% reported vacancy rates that exceeded 30% of staffing levels, with 166 of those centers reporting rates above 40%.\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered