(3727, 6, 'post', '707', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/press-releases/2B5E896F-D914-47DC-8D3B-304E6E2AD5A7', 'Seven Colorado Emergency Response Centers Earn  “Center of Excellence” Honors from the IAED', 50, 'done', 1, 1212, '', '{\"id\":707,\"date\":\"2023-04-18T15:43:39\",\"date_gmt\":\"2023-04-18T15:43:39\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/2B5E896F-D914-47DC-8D3B-304E6E2AD5A7\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T07:47:10\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T07:47:10\",\"slug\":\"2b5e896f-d914-47dc-8d3b-304e6e2ad5a7\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/2B5E896F-D914-47DC-8D3B-304E6E2AD5A7\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"Seven Colorado Emergency Response Centers Earn  \\u201cCenter of Excellence\\u201d Honors from the IAED\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The Colorado honorees are: &nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\\"wp-block-list\\\">\\n<li>Denver 911 in Denver, CO \\u00a0<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Colorado Springs Public Safety Communications in Colorado Springs, CO<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>El Paso County Sheriff\\u2019s Office in Colorado Springs, CO\\u00a0 \\u00a0\\u00a0<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Fort Collins 911 in Fort Collins, CO<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Loveland Emergency Communications Center in Loveland, CO<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>South Metro Fire Rescue in Centennial, CO<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Weld County Regional Communications Center in Greeley, CO<\\/li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">These agencies were recognized during IAED\\u2019s 2023 <a style=\\\"color:#0563c1;text-decoration:underline;\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/navigator.emergencydispatch.org\\/home\\\">NAVIGATOR<\\/a> conference in Denver, which is bringing together more than 1,500 emergency services leaders for continuing education and professional development.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/press-releases\\/8429ee86-cb0b-4350-8bf3-1932d7ab0fe2\\\">&gt;&gt; View the list of recipients by state<\\/a><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The IAED\\u2019s ACE credential is the highest distinction given to emergency communication centers, certifying that they are performing at or above global standards for best practices in emergency response. ACE centers have completed a rigorous set of 20 Points of Accreditation, including strong local oversight, rigorous quality processes, and a commitment to data-driven continuous improvement.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black;\\\">\\u201cAccreditation is truly a pinnacle achievement,\\u201d said Christof Chwojka, Accreditation Board Chair at IAED. \\u201cWe applaud the dedicated calltakers, dispatchers, and leaders at each of these agencies for their commitment to the highest standards, which few achieve. The ACE credential means Coloradans can count on their <\\/span><i><span style=\\\"color:black;\\\">first<\\/span><\\/i><span style=\\\"color:black;\\\"> first responders to do an outstanding job.\\u201d<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black;\\\">Accreditation is valid for a three-year period, during which all standards must be upheld. Emergency communication centers can earn multiple accreditations, one for each emergency discipline they service (medical, fire, police, and emergency nurse triage).<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><span style=\\\"color:black;\\\">Over 3,500 emergency communication centers worldwide use the medical, fire, police, and emergency nurse triage protocols developed and maintained by the IAED. The Priority Dispatch System<sup>TM&nbsp; <\\/sup>is recognized and used in 46 countries as the highest standard of care and practice for emergency dispatch.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">For more information about IAED accreditation, visit <a style=\\\"color:#0563c1;text-decoration:underline;\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/what-we-do\\/accreditation\\\">https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/what-we-do\\/accreditation<\\/a>.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><strong>About the IAED<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The IAED is the standard-setting organization for emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and is the leading body of emergency dispatch experts. Our various boards and councils work on behalf of over 69,000 members in 59 countries\\u2014and in coordination with other influential public safety organizations\\u2014to ensure that the comprehensive system of emergency dispatching is safe, fast, effective and cutting-edge. IAED protocols are used in more than 4,080 communications centers across the world and have been time-tested across hundreds of millions of calls for medical, fire, police, and nurse triage dispatching. Learn more at <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.emergencydispatch.org\\\">www.emergencydispatch.org<\\/a>.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\\\">###<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>April 18, 2023 (DENVER, Col.) \\u2014 The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u00ae (IAED), the standard-setting organization for emergency dispatch services worldwide, today announced that seven emergency dispatch centers in Colorado, staffed by teams of medical, fire, police, and emergency nurse triage responders, have earned or re-earned IAED\\u2019s Accredited Center of Excellence (ACE) designation.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[22],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-707\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-press-releases\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>Seven Colorado Emergency Response Centers Earn \\u201cCenter of Excellence\\u201d Honors from the IAED | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"Seven Colorado Emergency Response Centers Earn \\u201cCenter of Excellence\\u201d Honors from the IAED | Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"April 18, 2023 (DENVER, Col.) \\u2014 The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u00ae (IAED), the standard-setting organization for emergency dispatch services worldwide, today announced that seven emergency dispatch centers in Colorado, staffed by teams of medical, fire, police, and emergency nurse triage responders, have earned or re-earned IAED\\u2019s Accredited Center of Excellence (ACE) designation.\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/2B5E896F-D914-47DC-8D3B-304E6E2AD5A7\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:site_name\\\" content=\\\"Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:published_time\\\" content=\\\"2023-04-18T15:43:39+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:modified_ti