=708\"}],\"wp:term\":[{\"taxonomy\":\"category\",\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/categories?post=708\"},{\"taxonomy\":\"post_tag\",\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/tags?post=708\"}],\"curies\":[{\"name\":\"wp\",\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/api.w.org\\/{rel}\",\"templated\":true}]}}', '{\"source_id\":\"708\",\"source_url\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/08BC63B6-A134-4547-8794-BE994386D8AB\",\"dest_id\":1213,\"dest_url\":\"http:\\/\\/localhost:8888\\/rnd\\/2023\\/04\\/18\\/08bc63b6-a134-4547-8794-be994386d8ab\\/\",\"title\":\"Stephen Zipprich of Portland, Oregon Honored as  North America\\u2019s 911 Dispatcher of the Year\",\"author\":\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\",\"featured\":\"\",\"inline_images\":0,\"failed_images\":0,\"reused_images\":0,\"comments\":0,\"terms\":1,\"builders\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"fidelity\":\"rendered\",\"failed_urls\":[]}', '2026-10-21 06:54:47'),
(3729, 6, 'post', '709', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/press-releases/A44026A1-F2FB-4BCA-BB06-A4F63DC63759', 'Barbara Ireland of New Orleans, Louisiana Honored as  North America’s 911 Instructor of the Year', 50, 'done', 1, 1214, '', '{\"id\":709,\"date\":\"2023-04-18T15:12:00\",\"date_gmt\":\"2023-04-18T15:12:00\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/A44026A1-F2FB-4BCA-BB06-A4F63DC63759\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T07:50:53\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T07:50:53\",\"slug\":\"a44026a1-f2fb-4bca-bb06-a4f63dc63759\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/A44026A1-F2FB-4BCA-BB06-A4F63DC63759\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"Barbara Ireland of New Orleans, Louisiana Honored as  North America\\u2019s 911 Instructor of the Year\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><i><strong>April 18, 2023 (DENVER, Col.) <\\/strong><\\/i>\\u2014 Barbara Ireland, Deputy Chief, retired, New Orleans EMS, is being honored today as North America\\u2019s 911 Instructor of the Year by the International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u00ae (IAED), the standard-setting organization for emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and the leading body of emergency dispatch experts.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The award, given annually to a U.S. emergency dispatch instructor who exemplifies excellence in his or her work throughout the year, is being announced at the IAED\\u2019s 2023 <a style=\\\"color:#0563c1;text-decoration:underline;\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/navigator.emergencydispatch.org\\/home\\\">NAVIGATOR<\\/a> &nbsp;Conference in Denver. The annual conference brings together more than 1,500 emergency services leaders from across the country and the world to stay abreast of best practices in emergency dispatch protocols.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u201cBarbara Ireland has been instructing emergency medical dispatch [EMD] since 2008, during which time she has instructed more than 250 classes,\\u201d said Eric Fayad, IAED Associate Director of Instructor Services. \\u201cShe was quick to jump into remote instruction at the start of the pandemic, and she has since been appointed a senior instructor, tasked with mentoring new EMD instructor candidates. She also is one of the leading EMD Study Hall instructors, taking extra time to help students with review. Barbara is a fierce proponent of emergency protocols and is not afraid to take on additional assignments when needed.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">As a non-profit with worldwide reach, the IAED provides training, education, and certification for more than 70,000 emergency dispatchers in over 50 countries. The Instructor of the Year Award is one of the most distinctive awards presented by the IAED, created to identify and celebrate individuals who have made the most significant contributions throughout the year to further the education and training of other professionals in the field.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u201cEmergency dispatchers are the <i>first<\\/i> first responders, the voices we hear in our worst moments when help is needed,\\u201d said Pam Stewart, IAED Senior Director of Operations and Board of Certification Chair. \\u201cThe Instructor of the Year Award recognizes instructors who go above and beyond to train emergency dispatchers, so that they are well equipped, prepared and confident.\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">For more information about the IAED, visit <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.emergencydispatch.org\\\">www.emergencydispatch.org<\\/a>.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\"><strong>About the IAED<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u00a0The IAED is the standard-setting organization for emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and is the leading body of emergency dispatch experts. Our various boards and councils work on behalf of over 69,000 members in 59 countries\\u2014and in coordination with other influential public safety organizations\\u2014to ensure that the comprehensive system of emergency dispatching is safe, fast, effective and cutting-edge. IAED protocols are used in more than 4,080 communications centers across the world and have been time-tested across hundreds of millions of calls for medical, fire, police, and nurse triage dispatching. Learn more at <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.emergencydispatch.org\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">www.emergencydispatch.org<\\/a>.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\\\">###<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>Award honors a 911 instructor for excellence in training and education<\\/p>\\n<p>April 18, 2023 (DENVER, Col.) \\u2014 Barbara Ireland, Deputy Chief, retired, New Orleans EMS, is being honored today as North America\\u2019s 911 Instructor of the Year by the International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u00ae (IAED), the standard-setting organization for emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and the leading bo<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[22],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-709\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-press-releases\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>Barbara Ireland of New Orleans, Louisiana Honored as North America\\u2019s 911 Instructor of the Year | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"Barbara Ireland of New Orleans, Louisiana Honored as North America\\u2019s 911 Instructor of the Year | Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"Award honors a 911 instructor for excellence in training and education  April 18, 2023 (DENVER, Col.) \\u2014 Barbara Ireland, Deputy Chief, retired, New Orleans EMS, is being honored today as North America\\u2019s 911 Instructor of the Year by the International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u00ae (IAED), the standard-setting organization for emergency dispatch and response services worldwide and the leading bo\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/press-releases\\/A44026A1-F2FB-4BCA-BB06-A4F63DC63759\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:site_name\\\" content=\\\"Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:published_time\\\" content=\\\"2023-04-18T15:12:00+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:modified_time\\\" content=\\\"2026-10-19T07:50:53+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"author\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:card\\\" content=\\\"summary_large_image\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:label1\\\" content=\\\"Written by\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data1\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:label2\\\" content=\\\"Est. reading time\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data2\\\" content=\\\"2 minutes\\\" \\/>\\n<script type=\\\"application\\/ld+json\\\" class=\\\"yoast-schema-graph\\\">{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\