hor\":\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\",\"featured\":\"\",\"inline_images\":0,\"failed_images\":0,\"reused_images\":0,\"comments\":0,\"terms\":1,\"builders\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"fidelity\":\"rendered\",\"failed_urls\":[]}', '2026-10-21 06:55:12'),
(3838, 6, 'post', '821', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/protocol-updates/medicalupdate14-6', 'Announcing the Release of MPDS v14.6 (6/5/2026) in ProQA v5.1.1.56', 50, 'done', 1, 1323, '', '{\"id\":821,\"date\":\"2026-06-29T16:10:54\",\"date_gmt\":\"2026-06-29T16:10:54\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/medicalupdate14-6\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-06-29T16:10:54\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-06-29T16:10:54\",\"slug\":\"medicalupdate14-6\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/protocol-updates\\/medicalupdate14-6\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"Announcing the Release of MPDS v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026) in ProQA v5.1.1.56\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"<h4>ProQA v5.1.1.56 Protocol, Logic, and Software Updates<\\/h4>\\n<p>We&#8217;re pleased to announce the release of <strong>ProQA\\u00ae v5.1.1.56<\\/strong> which includes updates in all three disciplines: <strong>FPDS\\u00ae v8.3 (6\\/2\\/2026), MPDS\\u00ae v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026)<\\/strong>, and<strong> PPDS\\u00ae v7.3 (4\\/28\\/2026)<\\/strong>. Continue reading this email for a brief overview of changes included.<\\/p>\\n<p>For more details about the changes in this release, see the ProQA v5.1.1.56 Release Notes linked below by discipline with the Determinant Code Conversion Guide starting on page two of the latest versions. We&#8217;ve also included a direct link to the longer Update Presentations on the Emergency Dispatch Learning Portal in each discipline to facilitate group training in your center. Optimize your group training using this <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/s\\/9pptrqqgtr\\\">Training Coordinator Guide for ProQA Releases<\\/a>.<\\/p>\\n<p><i><strong>Note:<\\/strong> In order to earn individual CDE, the Update Presentations require course enrollment and completion\\u2014free of charge\\u2014on the Emergency Dispatch Learning Portal.<\\/i><\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Notice the Dot Version Numbers Look Different?<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<p>We want to remind you about the dot version number simplification you\\u2019re seeing with this release for the latest versions: FPDS v8.3 (6\\/2\\/2026), MPDS v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026), and PPDS v7.3 (4\\/28\\/2026).<\\/p>\\n<p>To review the explanation for these changes and also the full version release schedule (beginning this fall with the release of Medical v15.0), please see this link to the <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/s\\/vqfqqqhw9f\\/new-protocol-release-processes-for-2026\\\">January 2026 email<\\/a> that was sent.<\\/p>\\n<h4>FIRE<br \\/>&nbsp;<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e8f8050e476652685660b088d3fe17f59\\\">FPDS v8.3 (6\\/2\\/2026) Release Notes<\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e0b1fc861277f9e1dd8ef655d9516e476\\\">FPDS v8.3 (6\\/2\\/2026) <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/learn.prioritydispatch.net\\/?callbackUrl=\\/academy\\/my_learning\\/course\\/167858\\\">Update Presentation<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e28502ceca3fa776f5ded49d118b248e5\\\">FPDS v7.1.276 (3\\/2\\/2026)\\u202fRelease Notes<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>MEDICAL<br \\/>&nbsp;<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e4681f0fc9cb4edbd7fda3d255b993f04\\\">MPDS v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026)\\u202fRelease Notes<\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e16bdd73046409a284bcb3307dd30210d\\\">MPDS v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026)\\u202f<a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/learn.prioritydispatch.net\\/?callbackUrl=\\/academy\\/my_learning\\/course\\/167859\\\">Update Presentation<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e3fde86103c4c2934822d6602d8bbe9d8\\\">MPDS v13.3.469 (3\\/2\\/2026) Release Notes<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>POLICE<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"eb3404e4706b71c23935b6ab7bede8b51\\\">PPDS 7.3 (4\\/28\\/2026) Release Notes<\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"ec07ed26200e77ad1bea34e5826300510\\\">PPDS 7.3 (4\\/28\\/2026) <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/learn.prioritydispatch.net\\/?callbackUrl=\\/academy\\/my_learning\\/course\\/167857\\\">Update Presentation<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e20cc62e8bc42fd49bb0474e86aeca8e4\\\">PPDS 7.0.547 (4\\/17\\/2026) Release Notes<\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"ec3cc0ba6939aded50490cae8eb491127\\\">PPDS 6.4.170\\u202f(7\\/29\\/2024) &lt;&#8211; This is the same as the previous four releases<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p><strong>Note:<\\/strong> See your Regional Client Outreach contact information at the end of this email, as well as a link to update your email preferences.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>UPDATE NOW!<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Click below<\\/strong>\\u202fand use your\\u202f<strong>Emergency Dispatch Learning Portal\\u202f<\\/strong>login information to access the<strong>\\u202fSoftware Support Portal<\\/strong>\\u202fand download software files and access release documentation. You&#8217;ll be prompted to create a login if you don&#8217;t already have one.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>As soon as you sign in for the first time, Software Support is notified and working on granting you access.<\\/strong>\\u202fThis process\\u202fmay take 24 to 48 hours.\\u202f<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Add Contacts:<\\/strong> Once in the Portal you can click Account Management (top right) then scroll down to the \\u201cAdd New Contact\\u201d button (center) and click to\\u202f<strong>add colleagues from your agency who would like\\u202fto receive these communications about releases.<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<p><a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/support.prioritydispatch.net\\/s\\/article\\/5-1-1-53-Release-Content\\\"><strong>DOWNLOAD SOFTWARE UPDATE AND DOCUMENTATION<\\/strong><\\/a><\\/p>\\n<p>For help updating your software, please contact\\u202f<strong>Software Support at 866-777-3911<\\/strong>\\u202for email\\u202f<a href=\\\"mailto:software.support@prioritydispatch.net\\\">software.support@prioritydispatch.net<\\/a><\\/p>\\n<p><strong>SPECIAL LANGUAGE INFORMATION: <\\/strong>This ProQA v5.1.1.56 release includes North American, Canadian, Australian, New Zealand, Hong Kong, and UK English, as well as French and US Spanish. ProQA v5.1.56 will be released in all other languages on June 30, 2026, alongside the release of AQUA v7 in all languages and AQUA v8 in English dialects. The first-ever international rollout of AQUA v8 in all PDS languages will follow shortly thereafter, in July 2026.<\\/p>\\n<figure class=\\\"image\\\"><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" style=\\\"aspect-ratio:800\\/200;\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/content\\/35lu797e3j\\/jpeg\\/IAEFD_Web%20Asset%20Headers.jpeg?w=800&amp;h=200&amp;keep=c&amp;crop=yes&amp;color=ffffffff&amp;quality=80&amp;u=0ma0bx\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"200\\\"><\\/figure>\\n<h3>&nbsp;<\\/h3>\\n<h3>FPDS v8.3 (6\\/2\\/2026)<\\/h3>\\n<h4>Global<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e703fa4eae890aec3e954bc516e647029\\\">When people are sick or injured, the follow-up Key Question \\u201cHow <strong>many<\\/strong>?\\u201d was changed to more specific variations, such as \\u201cHow <strong>many<\\/strong>\\u202fpeople are <strong>sick<\\/strong>?\\u201d or \\u201cHow <strong>many<\\/strong>\\u202fpeople are <strong>injured<\\/strong>?\\u201d<\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e954e7f86b05313f031d8f4cdde4a1d17\\\">The PDI-b Pre-Instruction Qualifier \\u201c<strong>(Returning immediately to Key Questions)<\\/strong>\\u201d\\u202fwas changed to \\u201c<strong>(Returning to Key Questions)<\\/strong>\\u201d.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>Protocol 77: Traffic Collision\\/Transporation Incident<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e5d98b1589e751ae063b9854445bdaa60\\\">Several new suffixes were added to indicate when an electric vehicle is involved in an incident.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>Protocol V: Vehicle on Fire (Caller Inside)<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"ed8b9ec78bf0956bce92139001c8d73df\\\">The instructions in Protocol V were updated to accommodate emergency door release levers\\/buttons.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<figure class=\\\"image\\\"><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" style=\\\"aspect-ratio:800\\/200;\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/content\\/xpks4bbmah\\/jpeg\\/IAEMD_Web%20Asset%20Headers.jpeg?w=800&amp;h=200&amp;keep=c&amp;crop=yes&amp;color=ffffffff&amp;quality=80&amp;u=0ma0bx\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"200\\\"><\\/figure>\\n<h3>&nbsp;<\\/h3>\\n<h3>Medical v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026)<\\/h3>\\n<h4>Multiple Protocols<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e509f4ed40ac728a223ff2667a4d00cfd\\\">To address concern about being able to capture possible Ebola illness during the upcoming FIFA World Cup, a new Jurisdictionally Approved Question was added to Protocols 1, 18, 21, and 26 to automatically launch the EIDS Tool. The findings from the EIDS Tool can then be recorded. Additionally, Protocol 26 has a new suffix that identifies suspected Ebola illness<\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e5aca0309989c3e532abee1356db4fcb0\\\">Several changes were made to the various CPR Pre-Arrival Instructions to reflect updated standards of care. Most notably, this includes changing the age range for newborns (neonates) from &lt; 30 days to &lt; 1 day and the age range for infants to 1 day to &lt; 1 year.<\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e6d3450fec4224b7714ccb931c05b872d\\\">ProQA now defaults the cursor to the Control bleeding (external) DLS Link if a patient has both SERIOUS bleeding and is in arrest on Protocols 3, 4, 17, 22, 27, 29, and 30. A new Rule to support bleeding control over compressions in traumatic arrests was also added to those Chief Complaints as well as Protocols 7 and 21.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>&nbsp;<\\/h4>\\n<h4>Case Entry and Protocol 29: Traffic Collision\\/Transportation Incident<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e73e2b3b024a7c6d26816c31d5022ddfe\\\">\\u201cAccelerator Stuck &amp; Can\\u2019t Stop Vehicle\\u201d was added to the Case Entry fast track list. Several changes to the Accelerator Stuck &amp; Can\\u2019t Stop Vehicle Tool and Protocol 29 were made to better support this incident type in the MPDS and make it more consistent with the FPDS and PPDS.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>&nbsp;<\\/h4>\\n<h4>Protocol 24: Pregnancy\\/Childbirth\\/Miscarriage<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e45362ad7198f76edec0395531eb0047d\\\">Several changes were made to Protocol 24, including a new incident type for no\\/reduced fetal movement, new HIGH RISK complications, and a new Determinant Code for constant abdominal pain.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<figure class=\\\"image\\\"><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\" style=\\\"aspect-ratio:800\\/200;\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/content\\/itjev2l277\\/jpeg\\/IAEPD_Web%20Asset%20Headers.jpeg?w=800&amp;h=200&amp;keep=c&amp;crop=yes&amp;color=ffffffff&amp;quality=80&amp;u=0ma0bx\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"200\\\"><\\/figure>\\n<h3>&nbsp;<\\/h3>\\n<h3>Police v7.3 (4\\/28\\/2026)<\\/h3>\\n<h4>ProQA Admin Utility<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"ee9af26f007899021744b0575ca97f163\\\">In Police Admin \\u2013 Restricted Settings, the default setting for the Critical Apprehension DE (CADE) is now \\u201cOn\\u201d. This change will enable the Critical Apprehension DE for both new installs and existing clients. Please contact your PDC Police representative for questions on this feature.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>Protocol 105: Animal<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e0ce1ffd1bb14ee513f1635ee2039ac84\\\">A new &#8220;Wild animal encounter&#8221; Sub-Chief Complaint was added, along with a new set of Pre-Arrival Instructions to handle bear, cougar\\/mountain lion\\/bobcat, wolf\\/coyote,\\u202fand elk\\/moose encounters.<\\/li>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"ec36390476c1b2e170fd5cd88473f68da\\\">A new suffix H for &#8220;Hospital (healthcare facility) reporting&#8221; was added to support hospitals that report animal ATTACKS\\/MINOR BITES.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>Protocol 106: &nbsp;Assault\\/Sexual Assault\\/Shooting\\/Stabbing<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e706af2b6d40a5b35911751b1a97f4982\\\">New Sub-Chief\\u202fComplaints, definitions, and suffixes were added to address reports of LESS-LETHAL DEVICES\\/ITEMS and Accidental SHOOTINGS (self-inflicted).<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<h4>Protocol 107: Assist Other Agencies\\/Organizations<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-list-item-id=\\\"e57b8981fabc2e89bbb721363f0f36027\\\">This protocol was extensively overhauled to better address the kinds of support requests police agencies receive and which agencies request support. This includes new Determinant Codes, suffixes, and Key Question sequences, among other changes.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>Do you need some dedicated support at your agency? Your\\u202f<a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/s\\/v9gdn5lhcq\\\">Regional Client Outreach representative <\\/a>(RCO) is\\u202fstanding by to help you get current with the latest protocols, troubleshoot any issues, or answer any questions you have. Don&#8217;t hesitate to reach out to your RCO!<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Update Today.<\\/strong>\\u202fYour Emergency Dispatchers, First Responders, and community need to be using the latest advancements in the protocols to meet the safety needs of our modern world.<\\/p>\\n<p>We&#8217;re here to help you every step of the way.<\\/p>\\n<p>Sincerely,<\\/p>\\n<p>The<strong>\\u202fInternational Academies of Emergency Dispatch<\\/strong> and<strong>\\u202fPriority Dispatch Corp.<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>We&#8217;re pleased to announce the release of ProQA\\u00ae v5.1.1.56 which includes updates in all three disciplines: FPDS\\u00ae v8.3 (6\\/2\\/2026), MPDS\\u00ae v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026), and PPDS\\u00ae v7.3 (4\\/28\\/2026).<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[26],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-821\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-protocol-updates\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>Announcing the Release of MPDS v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026) in ProQA v5.1.1.56 | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"Announcing the Release of MPDS v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026) in ProQA v5.1.1.56 | Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"We&#039;re pleased to announce the release of ProQA\\u00ae v5.1.1.56 which includes updates in all three disciplines: FPDS\\u00ae v8.3 (6\\/2\\/2026), MPDS\\u00ae v14.6 (6\\/5\\/2026), and PPDS\\u00ae v7.3 (4\\/28\\/2026).\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/protocol-updates\\/medicalupdate14-6\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:site_name\\\" content=\\\"Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:published_time\\\" content=\\\"2026-06-29T16:10:54+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:image\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/content\\/35lu797e3j\\/jpeg\\/IAEFD_Web%20Asset%20Headers.jpeg?w=800&amp;h=200&amp;keep=c&amp;crop=yes&amp;color=ffffffff&amp;quality=80&amp;u=0ma0bx\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"author\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:card\\\" content=\\\"summary_large_image\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:label1\\\" content=\\\"Written by\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data1\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:label2\\\" content=\\\"Est. reading time\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data2\\\" content=\\\"5 minutes\\\" \\/>\\n<script type=\\\"application\\/ld+json\\\" class=\\\"yoast-schema-graph\\\">{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\\",\\\"@graph\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Article\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/in-the-news\\\\\\/protocol-updates\\\\\\/medicalupdate14-6\\\\\\/#article\\\",\\\"isPartOf\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/in-the-news\\\\\\/protocol-updates\\\\\\/medicalupdate14-6\\\\\\/\\\"},\\\"author\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/#\\\\\\/schema\\\\\\/person\\\\\\/338f35ee363eca7c9019764391474b5a\\\"},\\\"headline\\\":\\\"Announcing the Release of MPDS v14.6 (6\\\\\\/5\\\\\\/2026) in ProQA v5.1.1.56\\\",\\\"datePublished\\\":\\\"2026-06-29T16:10:54+00:00\\\",\\\"mainEntityOfPage\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/in-the-news\\\\\\/protocol-updates\\\\\\/medicalupdate14-6\\\\\\/\\\"},\\\"wordCount\\\":1092,\\\"commentCount\\\":0,\\\"image\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/in-the-news\\\\\\/protocol-updates\\\\\\/medicalupdate14-6\\\\\\/#primaryimage\\\"},\\\"thumbnailUrl\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\\\\\/content\\\\\\/35lu797e3j\\\\\\/jpeg\\\\\\/IAEFD_Web%20Asset%20Headers.jpeg?w=800&amp;h=200&amp;keep=c&amp;crop=yes&amp;color=ffffffff&amp;quality=80&amp;u=0ma0bx\\\",\\\"ar