(3886, 6, 'post', '870', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/protocol-updates/E3F0D409-7064-4962-A44E-F3C1EB24B132', 'IAED Announces Release of Police Version 5.0', 50, 'done', 1, 1371, '', '{\"id\":870,\"date\":\"2015-05-07T00:00:00\",\"date_gmt\":\"2015-05-07T00:00:00\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/E3F0D409-7064-4962-A44E-F3C1EB24B132\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T06:33:04\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T06:33:04\",\"slug\":\"e3f0d409-7064-4962-a44e-f3c1eb24b132\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/protocol-updates\\/E3F0D409-7064-4962-A44E-F3C1EB24B132\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"IAED Announces Release of Police Version 5.0\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u00ae (IAED\\u2122) announces a new version of the Police Protocol Dispatch System\\u2122 (PPDS\\u00ae) that will be officially released at NAVIGATOR 2015.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Version 5 is built upon the speed and precision of each preceding version to enhance the ability of emergency police dispatchers (EPDs) to gather the most appropriate and accurate information for their field responders.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">&#8220;We&#8217;ve concentrated on further protocol and software refinements in the dispatch process with innovations made possible through our software ProQA\\u00ae and the feedback we&#8217;ve received from our users,&#8221; IAED Police Consultant Dave Warner said. &#8220;We&#8217;re really excited about releasing Version 5 and, as always, hearing the feedback about how the system works for their agency.&#8221;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">PPDS v5.0 introduces two global features that places more control in the hands of the agencies. Improvements to Protocols 108 and 109 involving Bombs and Suspicious Packages \\u2013 found and threatened \\u2013 have been made as well as new Determinant Codes for Product Contamination and Product Contamination Threats.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Warner emphasized enhancements in Protocol 108: Bomb Threat\\/Product Contamination and Protocol 109: Suspicious Package (Letter, Item, Substance)\\/Product Contamination have been made to ensure an appropriate and conversational interrogation for these events that vary greatly from one another in the nature of the incident.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">\\u00a0&#8220;This is a great example of reordering questions to gather the information responders need for scene safety,&#8221; he said. &#8220;New questions pertaining to product contamination help further exposure to callers and bystanders before responders can secure the scene.&#8221;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">A big plus for agencies is the revision to the blue prompt used in gathering descriptive information, such as cultural identification. In v5.0, the blue prompt is dropped in favor of allowing the agency to develop suspect and vehicle descriptions most relevant to their demographics, and other variables, during EMD interrogation. A second global enhancement relies on the power of ProQA v5.1, which is the only software version available for operating PPDS v5.0. The new CAD\\/MDC (Mobile Data Computer) feature allows agencies to decide the information to turn on or turn off on the CAD based on a value system developed by the Academy. The feature, Key Question Answer Importance (KQAI), accelerates data flow relevant to the incident.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">&#8220;This is something our users have wanted,&#8221; Warner said. &#8220;It sets the amount and type of information necessary for the specific situation. We made it a priority in software to keep the information flow manageable and relevant.&#8221;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">For more information, go to the IAED Web site at <a href=\\\"\\/home\\\" class=\\\"inline-link\\\"> www.emergencydispatch.org<\\/a>.<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u00ae (IAED\\u2122) announces a<br \\/>\\nnew version of the Police Protocol Dispatch System\\u2122 (PPDS\\u00ae) that<br \\/>\\nwill be officially released at NAVIGATOR 2015. Version 5 is built upon the speed and precision&#8230;<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[26],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-870\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-protocol-updates\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>IAED Announces Release of Police Version 5.0 | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"IAED Announces Release of Police Version 5.0 | Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"The International Academies of Emergency Dispatch\\u00ae (IAED\\u2122) announces a new version of the Police Protocol Dispatch System\\u2122 (PPDS\\u00ae) that will be officially released at NAVIGATOR 2015. Version 5 is built upon the speed and precision...\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/protocol-updates\\/E3F0D409-7064-4962-A44E-F3C1EB24B132\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:site_name\\\" content=\\\"Emergency Dispatch\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:published_time\\\" content=\\\"2015-05-07T00:00:00+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:modified_time\\\" content=\\\"2026-10-19T06:33:04+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"author\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:card\\\" content=\\\"summary_large_image\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:label1\\\" content=\\\"Written by\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data1\\\" content=\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:label2\\\" content=\\\"Est. reading time\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta name=\\\"twitter:data2\\\" content=\\\"2 minutes\\\" \\/>\\n<script type=\\\"application\\/ld+json\\\" class=\\\"yoast-schema-graph\\\">{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/schema.org\\\",\\\"@graph\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Article\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/protocol-updates\\\\\\/E3F0D409-7064-4962-A44E-F3C1EB24B132\\\\\\/#article\\\",\\\"isPartOf\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/protocol-updates\\\\\\/E3F0D409-7064-4962-A44E-F3C1EB24B132\\\\\\/\\\"},\\\"author\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/#\\\\\\/schema\\\\\\/person\\\\\\/338f35ee363eca7c9019764391474b5a\\\"},\\\"headline\\\":\\\"IAED Announces Release of Police Version 5.0\\\",\\\"datePublished\\\":\\\"2015-05-07T00:00:00+00:00\\\",\\\"dateModified\\\":\\\"2026-10-19T06:33:04+00:00\\\",\\\"mainEntityOfPage\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\/\\\\\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\\\\\/news\\\\\\/protocol-updates\\\\\\/E3F0D409-7064-4962-A44E-F3C1EB24B132\\\\\\/\\\"},\\\"wordCount\\\":415,\\\"commentCount\\\":0,\\\"articleSection\\\":[\\\"Protocol Updates\\\"],\\\"inLanguage\\\":\\\"en-US\\\",\\\"potentialAction\\\":[{\\