s\\/76EC20C7-D63A-4F35-AF12-67BB61CA3B1A\",\"dest_id\":1389,\"dest_url\":\"http:\\/\\/localhost:8888\\/rnd\\/2012\\/08\\/21\\/76ec20c7-d63a-4f35-af12-67bb61ca3b1a\\/\",\"title\":\"Seamless, Immediate care\",\"author\":\"webdev@oozlemedia.com\",\"featured\":\"\",\"inline_images\":0,\"failed_images\":0,\"reused_images\":0,\"comments\":0,\"terms\":1,\"builders\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"fidelity\":\"rendered\",\"failed_urls\":[]}', '2026-10-21 06:55:26'),
(3905, 6, 'post', '889', 'https://emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com/news/agency-news/C17A1668-623D-4296-AEB9-57C6A5269477', 'In Memory of Dr. Laura Kay', 50, 'done', 1, 1390, '', '{\"id\":889,\"date\":\"2011-03-31T00:00:00\",\"date_gmt\":\"2011-03-31T00:00:00\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/in-the-news\\/uncategorized\\/C17A1668-623D-4296-AEB9-57C6A5269477\\/\"},\"modified\":\"2026-10-19T08:01:57\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2026-10-19T08:01:57\",\"slug\":\"c17a1668-623d-4296-aeb9-57c6a5269477\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"post\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/emergencydistg.wpenginepowered.com\\/news\\/agency-news\\/C17A1668-623D-4296-AEB9-57C6A5269477\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"In Memory of Dr. Laura Kay\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\\n<img decoding=\\\"async\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/prioritydispatch.widen.net\\/content\\/tx5i8050yr\\/webp\\/dr_laura_kay.webp?w=600&#038;position=c&#038;color=ffffff00&#038;quality=80&#038;u=wfnssn\\\" alt=\\\"dr_laura_kay\\\" >\\n\\n\\n\\n<p class=\\\"wp-block-paragraph\\\">Dr. Laura Kay was an amazing person. She was a professional role model, mother, friend, and physician. &#8220;She expected the best from herself and everyone that worked with her, and because of that, I felt like I was a better person,&#8221; wrote Natalie Frasure on the Facebook page dedicated to Dr. Kay. Frasure&#8217;s tribute genuinely represents the more than 100 messages posted in less than a week following the tragic death of the medical director for the Santa Fe Regional Emergency Dispatch Center. Dr. Kay was caring, a strong advocate for rural volunteer EMTs and firefighters. She was known for her energy, hard work, and direct approach. She didn&#8217;t mince words or feign flattery. &#8220;Those of us who got to know her were blessed with a good friend and staunch supporter,&#8221; according to friend and associate Donna McHenry. Dr. Kay died Thursday, March 24, 2011. She was 44 years old. Brett Patterson, IAED Academics and Standards Associate and Research Council Chair, was startled and deeply saddened by the news. &#8220;Laura\\\\&#8217;s last three days were spent teaching EMDs and consulting with me about ways to convince the powers that be in New Mexico to adopt the MPDS as a standard of care statewide,&#8221; said Patterson, who met Dr. Kay eight years ago at an EMD course he was teaching in Santa Fe. &#8220;After the last day of class on Wednesday afternoon \\\\[March 23\\\\], I gave her a hug and told her what a great job she had done. She died early Thursday morning.&#8221; Dr. Kay, a graduate of the University of Missouri, Columbia School of Medicine, was dedicated to EMS, Patterson said. As an advocate, she took the time to understand each link in the chain of response, including the details of the Medical Priority Dispatch System\\u2122 (MPDS\\u00ae) protocols. Her interest drew the attention of protocol inventor Jeff Clawson, M.D. She enthusiastically accepted his invitation to join the IAED Council of Standards. &#8220;The strong opinions she had about professional standards in EMS complemented the Academy&#8217;s goals,&#8221; Dr. Clawson said. &#8220;She understood the logic of the protocol and the benefits of the protocol for both the patient and the dispatcher.&#8221; Marie Leroux, Standards Council chair, praised Dr. Kay&#8217;s contributions to advocacy. &#8220;She was intent on going into the EMD community to reinforce the ideals she and her colleagues at the IAED supported,&#8221; Leroux said. &#8220;She will be greatly missed.&#8221; Dr. Kay fit the very definition of EMS. She was an emergency room physician in Kansas, Alamogordo, N.M. and Albuquerque, N.M. She received NAED EMD-Q certification in 2007. She was a member of the American Medical Association, a flight physician for Lifeguard Aero Medical Services-rotor &amp; fixed wing, a commissioner with the state EMS Licensing Commission, a member of the IAED Readers Group of the Council of Standards, a resident of Emergency Medicine of The University of New Mexico School of Medicine and medical director of the Santa Fe 911, Santa Fe Regional Emergency Communication Center. &#8220;May your legacy always be for all the positive things you did for EMS in New Mexico,&#8221; wrote Jesse Davis on the Facebook page. And, without a doubt, the legacy will be long remembered by the many people her dedication touched and inspired. You are encouraged to share any stories and photos you may have on this <a href=\\\"http:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/pages\\/Remembering-Dr-Laura-Kay\\/200266813326988\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Facebook page<\\/a>. These entries will be collected and made available to her children, Jacob and Sarah, as a memory book. <a href=\\\"http:\\/\\/www.facebook.com\\/pages\\/Remembering-Dr-Laura-Kay\\/200266813326988\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">REMEMBERING DR. LAURA KAY FACEBOOK LINK<\\/a><\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>Dr. Laura Kay was an amazing person. She was a professional<br \\/>\\nrole model, mother, friend, and physician.<\\/p>\\n<p>&#8220;She expected the best from herself and everyone that worked with her,<br \\/>\\nand because of that, I felt like I was a better person,&#8221; wrote Natalie&#8230;<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":1,\"featured_media\":0,\"comment_status\":\"open\",\"ping_status\":\"open\",\"sticky\":false,\"template\":\"\",\"format\":\"standard\",\"meta\":{\"_acf_changed\":false,\"footnotes\":\"\"},\"categories\":[27],\"tags\":[],\"class_list\":[\"post-889\",\"post\",\"type-post\",\"status-publish\",\"format-standard\",\"hentry\",\"category-agency-news\"],\"acf\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.7 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/product\\/yoast-seo-wordpress\\/ -->\\n<title>In Memory of Dr. Laura Kay | Emergency Dispatch<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"noindex, follow, max-s